The body-sensitivity check confirms the scope failure: I inserted an unconditional `return True`, producing a byte-different MPY that is wrong for `"("`; the unchanged submitted claim still proved `#Top`. That is direct evidence the K theorem does not pin the real program. I’m now running the separate required false-result mutation to establish that the internal loop theorem itself is non-vacuous.
